Feature: Capital call journey — undoing actions
  Actions that undo progress re-check the call's journey at once, move it back, and reset sign-offs
  on later tasks that were given before the undo started. Figure, date and email edits mark tasks
  stale, because their effect can't be seen in the data alone.
  Worked examples E7, E8, E10, E10b, E12, E13, E17, E18, E24 in
  openspec/changes/archive/2026-10-02-capital-call-journey/design.md#worked-examples

  Background:
    Given Im logged in as a user "" for an entity "entity_type=Investment Fund;enable_funds=true;currency=INR"
    And the user has role "company_admin"
    And the user has role "approver"
    And there is an existing investor "" with "1" users
    And there is an existing investor "" with "1" users
    And there is a fund "name=Alpha Fund I" for the entity
    And the investors are added to the fund
    And there are capital commitments of "orig_folio_committed_amount_cents=100000000" from each investor
    And each investor has a "verified" kyc linked to the commitment
    And the entity's capital call journeys are seeded
    And the fund has capital call template

  # E8 — a figures edit resets the CFO sign-off
  Scenario: Editing the call's figures moves back to Create remittances and resets the CFO sign-off
    Given the Full journey has a "CFO sign-off" approval step before "Approve call"
    And there is a capital call "percentage_called=10"
    And the call is ready for sign-off and the CFO has signed off
    When I change the call's percentage called to "12"
    Then the call's journey current task should be "Create remittances"
    And the call's journey message for "Create remittances" should be "Remittances were calculated before the call figures changed — recompute"
    And the CFO vote on step "CFO sign-off" should be archived
    And the user should receive a sign-off reset email mentioning "Call figures changed"

  # E13 — recompute, then the notices are stale
  Scenario: After a figures edit, Recompute Call passes the remittances and marks the notices stale
    Given there is a capital call "percentage_called=10"
    And the call is ready for sign-off
    When I change the call's percentage called to "12"
    And I recompute the call
    Then the call's journey should show:
      | task               | status  |
      | Create remittances | passed  |
      | Generate notices   | current |
    And the call's journey message for "Generate notices" should be "Notices were generated before the remittances changed — unapprove them on the Documents screen, then click Generate Documents"

  # E7 — unapprove the notices, then regenerate (later review confirmations are reset)
  Scenario: Unapproving a notice moves back to Approve notices and regenerating keeps it there
    Given there is a capital call "percentage_called=10"
    And the call is ready for sign-off
    When I unapprove one of the call's notices on the Documents screen
    Then the call's journey current task should be "Approve notices"
    And the history should show "regressed" for step "Approve notices"
    When the call's notices are regenerated by the doc job
    Then the call's journey current task should be "Approve notices"
    And the "Review custom notification" confirmation should have been reset

  # E10 — undo and redo before anyone looks
  Scenario: Unapproving and re-approving a notice still resets the later CFO sign-off
    Given the Full journey has a "CFO sign-off" approval step before "Approve call"
    And there is a capital call "percentage_called=10"
    And the call is ready for sign-off and the CFO has signed off
    When I unapprove one of the call's notices on the Documents screen
    And I approve that notice again
    Then the history should show "regressed" for step "Approve notices"
    And the CFO vote on step "CFO sign-off" should be archived

  # E10b — unapprove the call keeps the earlier CFO sign-off
  Scenario: Unapproving the call moves back to Approve call and keeps the earlier sign-off
    Given the Full journey has a "CFO sign-off" approval step before "Approve call"
    And there is a capital call "percentage_called=10"
    And the call is ready for sign-off and the CFO has signed off
    And when the capital call is approved
    And the call's journey is evaluated
    When I unapprove the call
    Then the call's journey current task should be "Approve call"
    And the history should show "regressed" for step "Approve call"
    And the CFO vote on step "CFO sign-off" should be kept

  # E12 — editing the email after review
  Scenario: Editing the fund's call email resets the email reviews
    Given there is a capital call "percentage_called=10"
    And the fund has a capital call email
    And the call is ready for sign-off
    When I edit the fund's capital call email
    Then the call's journey current task should be "Review custom notification"
    And the call's journey message for "Review custom notification" should be "Email template changed after review"

  # E24 — an email edit after sending leaves the sent call alone
  Scenario: Editing the fund's call email only affects calls not yet sent
    Given the fund has a capital call email
    And there is a capital call "percentage_called=10"
    And the call is ready for sign-off
    And the call's notices are marked sent
    And the call's journey is evaluated
    And I remember this call as "call A"
    And there is a capital call "name=Second call;percentage_called=5"
    And the call is ready for sign-off
    When I edit the fund's capital call email
    Then the call's journey current task should be "Review custom notification"
    And the journey of "call A" should not have moved back

  # E17 — undo on a call without a journey
  Scenario: Editing a call that has no journey works as before
    Given the entity's capital call journeys are removed
    And there is a capital call "percentage_called=10"
    When I change the call's percentage called to "12"
    Then the call should be saved with percentage called "12"
    And the call has no journey

  # E18 — unverify reopens a completed journey
  Scenario: Unverifying a remittance reopens a completed journey
    Given there is a capital call "percentage_called=10"
    And the call has no unit prices
    And the call is ready for sign-off
    And when the capital call is approved
    And the call's notices are marked sent
    And the call's remittances are fully paid
    And the call's remittances are verified
    And the call's journey is evaluated
    And the call's journey should be complete
    When I unverify one of the call's remittances
    Then the call's journey current task should be "Verify remittances"
    And the history should show "reopened" for step "Verify remittances"
